=== OLS vs lasso CO_Mega model, ribonn TE, LCL ===

[1] Coefficients
  lasso alpha (10-fold CV, standardized predictors) = 0.000908
  lasso keeps 59 of 61 codons; sets 2 to exactly 0: TAT, ATT
  of those 2, 0 are nominally significant (p < 0.05) in the OLS model; OLS has 18 nominally significant codons overall, 18 of them kept by the lasso
  OLS vs lasso coefficients: Pearson r = 0.9998, Spearman rho = 0.9993; slope of lasso on OLS among kept codons = 0.988 (shrinkage)
  coefficient mean / SD across the 61 codons: OLS -43.878 / 6.574, lasso -1.324 / 6.495
  NOTE: the 61 sense-codon frequencies of a gene sum to ~1 (see [2]), so together with the intercept the OLS
  coefficients are only identified up to a common shift (add c to every coefficient, subtract c from the
  intercept): the huge OLS intercept / mean coefficient are that arbitrary shift, not an effect. Only the
  differences between codons (SD, correlations, slope above, all shift-invariant) are meaningful; the lasso
  penalty picks the sparse solution, which is why its intercept and mean coefficient stay small.
  intercept: OLS 43.6785, lasso 1.1262

[2] Fit on 9,776 autosomal training genes
